notes: V038 is an owner-requested new patch after V037. It keeps the V037/R6 quality-preserving ESP camera firmware and aitl-tcp-jpeg-v1 wire protocol unchanged, while adding a built-in Camera Diagnostics page and backend diagnostic service. One Diagnose action runs staged evidence checks against the currently selected saved ESP camera: repeated direct /status control probes; firmware/camera-readiness/Wi-Fi telemetry checks; a direct ATL1/JPEG stream phase that bypasses the normal PC Studio stream worker; a second direct stream phase with concurrent /status polling; and a normal RemoteCameraManager/RemoteCameraService managed-stream phase. The diagnostic temporarily quiesces the selected stream/simulation when needed, uses the saved camera image settings at a conservative 5 FPS during measurement, then restores the previous saved FPS/settings and connection/simulation state. Results classify likely failures such as control-unreachable, firmware mismatch, camera-not-ready, ESP camera/TCP send stall, HTTP-control/stream contention, PC Studio receiver/session integration, weak Wi-Fi margin, or healthy-now, and expose measured evidence rather than requiring a separate command-line test. No new stable error code, ESP-side inference, UDP transport, permanent camera-profile setting change, or physical/public-road signal authority is introduced. V024 / 0_2_4 remains the owner-confirmed passed baseline until explicit owner acceptance changes it.
